## API access available
Keys live in `~/.claude/.env` (chmod 600). Names only here — never values.

| Service | Env var | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| Meshy AI | `MESHY_API_KEY` | `https://api.meshy.ai/openapi/v1/...`, Bearer auth. Balance checked 2026-09-08: 1300 credits |
| Sketchfab | `SKETCHFAB_API_TOKEN` | Used by the `sketchfab` CLI |
| Freesound | `FREESOUND_API_KEY`, `FREESOUND_CLIENT_ID` | Both from one application at `freesound.org/apiv2/apply`. The API key doubles as the OAuth client secret. Token auth gives search plus 128k mp3 previews; original WAVs need the one-time `sfx auth` login, which caches a refresh token in `~/.claude/.freesound-token.json` |
| ElevenLabs | `ELEVENLABS_API_KEY` | **The key is not in `~/.claude/.env`** — checked 2026-09-17, the API returns 401 `needs_authorization`. Anything planning to use it must add the key first or fall back. `POST https://api.elevenlabs.io/v1/sound-generation`, `xi-api-key` header. The free tier grants no commercial rights, so a paid plan is required for anything we might sell |

## Known gaps in local tools

- **Godot will not import a 24-bit WAV.** Freesound originals are often 24-bit, and the
  `sfx` tool saves them as downloaded, so the import fails with "Format not supported for
  WAVE file (not PCM)" and the game loads nothing. Convert each one and load the
  conversion: `ffmpeg -y -i original.wav -acodec pcm_s16le -ar 44100 shutter.wav`. Keep the
  originals for provenance and drop a `.gdignore` in their folder so Godot stops trying.
  Found in `snapshot`, 2026-09-17.
- **Godot's `class_name` globals need `--import` after editing scripts from outside the
  editor.** The list lives in `.godot/global_script_class_cache.cfg`, and until it is
  rebuilt every `class_name` fails with "Could not find type X in the current scope" -
  which reads like a syntax error and is not one. Run
  `Godot --headless --path . --import` once after creating script files with anything
  other than the editor. Found in `snapshot`, 2026-09-17.
- **ffmpeg has no `drawtext` and no `subtitles` filter.** The Homebrew build (9.0.1) was compiled
  without libfreetype and libass, so text cannot be burned in by a filter at all. Check with
  `ffmpeg -filters | grep drawtext` before planning on it. The way round it is to draw frames with
  PIL and pipe raw RGB24 into ffmpeg, which only encodes — see `projects/shorts-factory/04-methods.md`.

## Tried & abandoned
| Tool | When | Why we stopped |
|---|---|---|
| Pixabay audio | 2026-09-09 | Their API exposes images and video endpoints only. The 130k sound effects on the website are not reachable programmatically, so it cannot be automated |
| Jamendo | 2026-09-09 | Free downloads are licensed for personal use only, which is unsafe for a game that might be sold |

## Local tools Claude can drive

| Tool | How | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| `sfx` | `sfx search "whistle" --max-sec 2` · `sfx get <id>` · `sfx make "wooden bat hit" -d 1.5 --wav` · `sfx packs` · `sfx pack ui-audio` | At `~/.local/bin/sfx`. One tool over Freesound, ElevenLabs and Kenney. Defaults to CC0 only; `--any-license` widens it to CC-BY. Saves into `<project>/assets/audio/` when run inside a Godot project, and appends every file to a `SOURCES.md` so provenance and licence are always traceable. |
| `rojo` | `rojo init` · `rojo build -o game.rbxlx` · `rojo serve` | v7.7.0. Keeps a Roblox game as Luau files on disk so it lives in git, and live-syncs into Studio through the Rojo Studio plugin. `rojo build` produces a place file with Studio closed. |
| `lune` | `lune run script.luau` | v0.10.5. Standalone Luau runtime — lets Claude execute and test Luau logic without opening Studio. |
| `stylua` / `selene` | `stylua src/` · `selene src/` | v2.5.2 / v0.31.0. Luau formatter and linter. |
| `wally` | `wally install` | v0.3.2. Roblox package manager. |
| macOS `say` | `say -v Samantha -r 172 --data-format=LEI16@22050 -o line.wav "text"` | Free offline text-to-speech, no key and no quota. `say -v '?'` lists installed voices; only the basic ones are here, and **Premium** voices are a large free quality gain via System Settings → Accessibility → Spoken Content → Manage Voices. It reports no word timings, so render each line to its own file and measure it with `ffprobe` (the pattern used in `shorts-factory`). The format must match the extension — `LEI16` needs `.wav`, not `.aiff`. |
| `texturelabs` | `texturelabs categories` · `texturelabs search wood` · `texturelabs pick metal -n 3` · `texturelabs get metal_167` · `texturelabs sync` | At `~/.local/bin/texturelabs`. Surface textures from texturelabs.org — no key, no account. Downloads land in `<project>/assets/texturelabs/` inside a project, and every file is recorded in a `SOURCES.md` beside it with the licence line. Only the "S" size is served publicly, and it is 1920 px despite the site calling it small. **Never commit the files** |
| Phaser API reference | `grep -n 'setVelocity' ~/Documents/dev/tools/phaser-api/node_modules/phaser/types/phaser.d.ts` | Phaser 4.2.1 installed as a plain npm package purely so the full typed API is readable offline. It is a reference copy, not a project — a real Phaser game gets its own `npm install phaser` in its own folder. |
| Codex CLI | `codex` in a project folder · `codex exec "task"` for one-shot, non-interactive runs | OpenAI's terminal coding agent, v0.155.0 (checked 2026-09-18; the latest release then). A standalone build at `~/.local/bin/codex` (symlink into `~/.codex/packages/standalone/`), not via npm or Homebrew. Signed in with Luqman's ChatGPT account, so usage counts against that plan rather than an API key. `codex login status` checks the sign-in. **Set up like Claude Code on 2026-09-19:** runs with no prompts and no sandbox (`approval_policy = "never"`, `sandbox_mode = "danger-full-access"` in `~/.codex/config.toml`), with Claude's deny list (sudo, rm -rf, git reset --hard, git clean, force-push) blocked in `~/.codex/rules/default.rules`. `~/.codex/.env` is a symlink to `~/.claude/.env`, so there is one key file. `~/.codex/AGENTS.md` is generated by `codex-sync` from `~/.claude/CLAUDE.md` plus the Claude memory files, and refreshed on every Codex start. `~/.codex/hooks.json` runs the Sky AI Brain recall on start and the portfolio-sync reminder after edits. The same MCP servers (godot, phaser-game-agent — Phaser's token is `PHASER_MCP_TOKEN` in the .env) and the docx/pdf/pptx/xlsx skills. Old config backed up in `~/Documents/dev/backups/codex-2026-09-19/`. |
| Aseprite | `"$HOME/Library/Application Support/Steam/steamapps/common/Aseprite/Aseprite.app/Contents/MacOS/aseprite" -b --script x.lua` | v1.3.18.3-arm64, installed via Steam (not `/Applications`). Full Lua API: sprites, layers, frames, tags, palettes. Export sheets with `--sheet` + `--data --format json-array`; preview with `--scale 8`. Claude reads the exported PNG back to check its own work. |

## Game engines and their MCP servers

| Engine | MCP server | What Claude can do | Limit |
|---|---|---|---|
| Godot | `godot-mcp` at `~/Documents/dev/tools/godot-mcp`, configured in `~/.claude.json` and `~/.codex/config.toml` | Create scenes, add nodes, save, run the project, read debug output | Cannot see the game |
| Roblox Studio | Official, built into Studio — Assistant Settings → MCP Servers → *Enable Studio as MCP server* | Create objects, set properties, write script sources, execute Luau, read the data model | Studio must stay open; cannot see the game |
| Phaser | `phaser-game-agent`, remote HTTP at `https://mcp.phaser.io/agent/mcp`, configured in `~/.claude.json` and `~/.codex/config.toml` (installed 2026-09-17) | Opens a sandbox project and builds a playable HTML5 game, including generated art and audio | **Costs money.** ~500 credits for a typical game build, billed per-minute of sandbox time plus generation. Account balance is 0, so `status` reports `access: NO` until credits are bought at <https://phaser.io/credits> |

The structural difference is that a Godot project is text on disk (`.tscn`, `.gd`),
so it can be built with the editor closed and committed to git as-is. A Roblox
project is a live Studio session or a binary `.rbxl`. Rojo closes that gap by
keeping the Luau on disk and syncing it in.

In both cases Claude is blind to how the game looks and feels. Luqman plays it and
reports back — that is the loop.

